<worksheet >
    <title>MD-1 Matrix Operations</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete all four parts. 
      Complete any three parts to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
   <page>
    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
        <introduction><p>Given the following matrices:
          <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="3">
          <mrow>X=\begin{bmatrix} 1 &amp; 1 \\ 2 &amp; 3 \end{bmatrix}, 
            Y=\begin{bmatrix} 4 &amp; -1 \\ -2 &amp; 1 \end{bmatrix}, 
            Z=\begin{bmatrix} 2 &amp; 2 \\ 4 &amp; 4 \end{bmatrix}, 
            W=\begin{bmatrix} 3 &amp; 1 &amp; 0 \\ 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 1 \end{bmatrix}</mrow>
        </md>
            Compute the following matrices, if possible.  If the computation is not 
            possible, explain why.</p></introduction>
      <task><statement><p><m>Z^{-1}</m></p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p><m>X^T-Y</m></p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p><m>XY+YX</m></p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p><m>W^3</m></p></statement></task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>